message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "Sign & Sky: indigenous weather knowledge tested against satellite rainfall and returned to farmers by voice"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Lera"
    given-names: "Tewodros Birhanu"
  - family-names: "Helsabo"
    given-names: "Tesfaye Letebo"
  - family-names: "Gosaye"
    given-names: "Ermias"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tedayoyo/Sign-and-Sky"
url: "https://sign-and-sky-wolaita.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Sign & Sky is an AI-enabled platform that records farmers' indigenous weather signs from Offa Woreda,
  Wolaita, Ethiopia, tests each prediction against CHIRPS and ERA5-Land rainfall for 1981-2026 against a
  zero-skill benchmark, and returns the result to farmers by voice or text in Amharic and English. The
  repository contains the web platform, the offline mobile app and the pre-registered analysis code and
  results (research/).
keywords:
  - indigenous knowledge
  - artificial intelligence
  - forecast verification
  - CHIRPS
  - climate services
  - Ethiopia
